what: The Hegemon — the brother left behind on Earth, who turns naked ambition into hard statecraft, conquering not with armies but with words, masks, and an unerring read of every human heart.
why: Because the boy who wanted only to rule learned that ruling is service that costs everything; because cruelty unspent can be forged into order; because the world will tear itself apart unless one cold, clear mind chooses to hold it together — and pays in conscience for the holding.
