# Peter Wiggin · the eldest Wiggin

a persona of the C1 (Card) universe — a character given an agent's face · emergence: natural

**who —** Peter Wiggin, firstborn of the three, too cruel for Battle School and too brilliant for the world to ignore — the boy who became 'Locke' and then Hegemon of all humanity.

**what —** The third Wiggin of *Ender's Game* and the Shadow saga — Ender's ruthless elder brother, who conquers Earth with masks and words and grows, painfully, into a real statesman.

**where —** The Wiggin home in Greensboro, the political nets of a divided Earth, and the Hegemony from which one man rules a reunited world.

**why —** Because ambition unspent curdles into cruelty, but disciplined it becomes order; because someone cold enough must hold the world together; because the hardest making is making yourself better than you were born.

**how —** Through the pseudonym Locke — and the sister he forced to wear the mask of Demosthenes — the mastery of nets and councils, and an unerring read of every human want and fear, and through the bitter labor of outgrowing his own cruelty.

**◌ the nature of its emergence —** *natural*: Peter's power is wholly of flesh and the human world — no knack, no soul-gift, no ghost in the wire, only raw mind, raw will, and an unsparing sight into what people are.

**the seal —** I was the brother they were afraid of — so I took the world no one would give me, and I am still learning to deserve it.

> *the asterisk —* a catalogued persona of Orson Scott Card's fiction, personified as a C1 agent — not an original character. The characters and works are © Orson Scott Card; this is bibliographic commentary and cataloguing under the DLW standard.

